-- Boot + behaviour smoke test for this package.
--
-- Two assertions, both in scope of the publish sandbox:
--
-- 1. register_with_config returns without runtime panic. Catches the
--    class of bugs that pass `ailang check` but crash at runtime —
--    pattern matches against the wrong ADT (e.g. matching Result
--    constructors against an Option value, std/json.getString returns
--    Option not Result, the original 0.1.1 code had this), readFile
--    panics when defaults aren't present, cross-package ADT shape
--    drift.
--
-- 2. summarize_with_ai handles Err(AIError) gracefully. The publish
--    sandbox runs without an AI provider configured, so step() returns
--    Err(AIError{code:"ProviderNotFound"}). Pre-0.1.4 the function
--    accessed .message.content directly on the Result, which auto-
--    unwrapped Err to .message:string, then crashed on .content with
--    "cannot access field of non-record value: *eval.StringValue".
--    The 0.1.4 match-discipline fix returns a fallback string starting
--    with "[summarizer unavailable:". This smoke pins that contract so
--    a future regression of the same shape would fail at publish time
--    instead of in arniwesth's agent loop at step 42.
--
-- Convention: every motoko-ext-* package SHOULD ship a _smoke.ail.
-- The parent Makefile :: verify-extensions iterates over packages/
-- motoko-ext-* and runs each _smoke.ail in isolation (process-per-
-- package, so a panic in pkg A doesn't mask pkg B's status).

module sunholo/motoko_ext_compaction_ai/_smoke

import std/io (println)
import std/string (length, contains)
import pkg/sunholo/motoko_ext_compaction_ai/register (register_with_config)
import pkg/sunholo/motoko_ext_compaction_ai/compaction_ai (summarize_with_ai)

export func main() -> () ! {AI, IO, Process, FS, Env, Net, SharedMem, Clock, Stream} {
  -- Assertion 1: register_with_config doesn't panic
  let _ = register_with_config(0);
  println("OK: register_with_config returned without panic");

  -- Assertion 2: summarize_with_ai handles the no-AI-handler Err path.
  -- In the publish sandbox no AI provider is configured, so step()
  -- returns Err(AIError{...}) and we expect the fallback string to
  -- come back. Pre-0.1.4 this would crash with *eval.StringValue.
  let result = summarize_with_ai("hello", "anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5");
  if length(result) == 0 then {
    println("FAIL: summarize_with_ai returned empty string (expected fallback)")
  } else {
    if contains(result, "[summarizer unavailable:") then {
      println("OK: summarize_with_ai returned fallback string on Err path")
    } else {
      -- If we got a real answer back the sandbox actually had an AI
      -- handler — print the result so the publisher knows. Not a
      -- failure (the bug class would have crashed by now anyway).
      println("OK: summarize_with_ai returned real text (sandbox had AI handler):");
      println(result)
    }
  }
}
